    "raw_text": "Network & Connectivity FAQ\nDomain: Basic network and internet troubleshooting.\nDataset purpose: This document is a sample knowledge-base source for a Multimodal\nRetrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) FAQ system.\nThe visual above is intentionally embedded so the data-extraction module can detect and extract images from the PDF.\nQ1. Why does my device show 'No Internet'?\nFirst check whether other devices can access the internet. If all devices are affected, restart the router and\ncheck the service connection. If only one device is affected, reconnect that device to the network.\nQ2. How can I reconnect to Wi-Fi?\nOpen the device's network settings, select the required Wi-Fi network, enter the correct password, and\nreconnect.\nQ3. Why is my internet connection slow?\nPossible causes include a weak wireless signal, many connected devices, background downloads, or\nnetwork service issues. Move closer to the router and test the connection again.\nQ4. What should I check before contacting support?\nRecord the device name, network name, approximate time of the problem, error message, and whether\nother devices are also affected.\nReference Information\nItem\nInformation to record\n\nDevice\nLaptop, desktop, phone, or tablet\nNetwork\nWi-Fi or wired connection\nError\nExact error message if displayed\nTime\nApproximate time the problem started\nSource type: Synthetic sample FAQ document | Suitable for local development and extraction testing.",
